      "date_verified": true,
      "discovered_at": "2026-07-25T08:23:38.442362Z",
      "category": "fan",
      "summary": "🚨 Oscar Piastri on if he feels he's the passenger of an AI program when it comes to the PUs \"Sometimes, yes. ...The principle of driving a race car that loses effectively half of its power before the end of the straight is hard to get your head around sometimes.\" \"Even in Spa, a lot of the middle sector we were doing it just on the combustion engine, with no battery assistance at all, which is a weird feeling in itself, having some corners with a certain amount of power & others with full power. I think Spa was particularly frustrating, not just for me but for quite a lot of others, because those small differences in the code & what the engines did made quite a big difference in lap time. Especially at the front of the field, I think there were still only 9 hundredths or something separating 4 positions & there were definitely more than 9 hundredths on the table for quite a few drivers with nothing they could control.\"",
      "summary_zh": "Oscar Piastri(Oscar Piastri)说,如果他觉得自己是一个AI程序的乘客,当涉及到PU\"有时,是的\". . . . . . . . 驾驶一辆在直道末端前有效失去一半功率的跑车的原则,有时很难得到你的头\". \"即使在斯帕,许多中产地 我们只是在燃烧机上做, 完全没有电池援助, 这本身就是一种奇怪的感觉, 有一些角落有一定功率, 另一些角落有全能。 我认为Spa特别令人沮丧, 不仅对我来说,而且对很多其他人来说, 因为代码和引擎的细微差异 在轮圈时间上有很大的不同。 特别是球场前方, 我认为仍然只有九百分之一,",
